'' windows-x86_64: the unnumbered in the LLVM list as declared, the numbered in .CRT$XCV /
'' .CRT$XTY plus 65535 minus the number. tiko-rt walks .CRT$XC* backwards and .CRT$XT*
'' forwards (lib/rt/src/c/msvccrt.c), which is fbc's order. A written 65535 is
'' unnumbered. See the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/structor-order.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal constant ptr @"P200", section ".CRT$XCV65335", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal constant ptr @"P101", section ".CRT$XCV65434", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal constant ptr @"Q101", section ".CRT$XTY65434", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.global_ctors = appending global [4 x { i32, ptr, ptr }] [{ i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"A1", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"B2", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"C3", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"P65535", ptr null }]
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.global_dtors = appending global [2 x { i32, ptr, ptr }] [{ i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"D1", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"D2", ptr null }]
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.used = appending global [3 x ptr]
